-- title:
--   Distinct minimal primes over a uniformiser are comaximal
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $B$ be a commutative $A$-algebra which is formally smooth over $A$ and of finite type over $A$. Let $\varpi \in A$ be an irreducible element, and let $P, P'$ be ideals of $B$, each minimal among the primes containing the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $B$, i.e. $P$ and $P'$ both lie in $(\mathrm{span}\{\,\text{algebraMap}\ A\ B\ \varpi\,\})$`.minimalPrimes`, that is, each is a prime ideal containing $\varpi B$ and minimal with this property. Assume $P \neq P'$. Then $P \sqcup P' = \top$, i.e. $P + P' = B$: the two ideals are comaximal, so they are contained in no common maximal ideal. Geometrically: two distinct generic points of irreducible components of the special fibre $\operatorname{Spec}(B/\varpi B)$ have disjoint closures.
--
--   This is the statement that distinct irreducible components of the special fibre of a smooth finite-type algebra over a discrete valuation ring do not meet, in the ideal-theoretic form used for local analysis of the reduction of models. It is invoked in the study of a rigid framed chart of a modular curve at auxiliary level, where it feeds the construction of the quotient field and the integral closedness of rings of invariants attached to such charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_FormallySmooth_sup_eq_top_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_isDiscreteValuationRing.lean

